.TH SDL_AudioStream 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_AudioStream \- The opaque handle that represents an audio stream.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_audio.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef struct SDL_AudioStream SDL_AudioStream;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION

.BR SDL_AudioStream
is an audio conversion interface\[char46]
.PP

\(bu It can handle resampling data in chunks without generating artifacts, when it doesn\(aqt have the complete buffer available\[char46]
.PP
\(bu It can handle incoming data in any variable size\[char46]
.PP
\(bu It can handle input/output format changes on the fly\[char46]
.PP
\(bu It can remap audio channels between inputs and outputs\[char46]
.PP
\(bu You push data as you have it, and pull it when you need it; the stream will buffer data as needed\[char46]
.PP
\(bu It can also function as a basic audio data queue even if you just have sound that needs to pass from one place to another\[char46]
.PP
\(bu You can hook callbacks up to them when more data is added or requested, to manage data on-the-fly\[char46]
.PP
Audio streams are the core of the SDL3 audio interface\[char46] You create one or more of them, bind them to an opened audio device, and feed data to them (or for recording, consume data from them)\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This struct is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_CreateAudioStream (3)
